{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg73izLq9G7rk151svZSV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, you can try Firecrawl for free, and you don't need a card.\n\nAccording to Firecrawl's pricing page, the free plan costs $0 and needs no credit card. It includes:\n- 1,000 credits per month, which their FAQ describes as about 1,000 pages.\n- 2 concurrent requests and low rate limits.\n- No rollover, so unused credits expire.\n\nSome third-party sites say the free tier is a one-time 500 or 1,000 credits. Those look out of date, and I trust the official page more. I only saw search-result summaries, not the pricing page itself, so check it before you rely on the numbers. Paid plans start at the Hobby tier.\n\nSources:\n- [Firecrawl pricing (official)](https://www.firecrawl.dev/pricing)\n- [Firecrawl pricing.md](https://www.firecrawl.dev/pricing.md)\n- [eesel.ai: Firecrawl pricing](https://www.eesel.ai/blog/firecrawl-pricing)\n- [webscraping.ai: Firecrawl free tier](https://webscraping.ai/faq/firecrawl/is-firecrawl-free-and-what-are-the-free-tier-limitations)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":885,"cache_read_input_tokens":18669,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":885},"output_tokens":402,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"318d8ce1-2db4-474f-839b-1cf4000d8f84","uuid":"d66b6d90-2980-48ac-bd22-15c44607f502","timestamp":"2026-10-17T02:49:14.536Z","request_id":"req_011Cg73iz6wpSkpZ2RWAvJZP"}
